# NOTICE

BargainProxy bundles or adapts code and protocol knowledge from the following
projects. Attribution and license compliance:

## Ported code / assets (MIT — code copied or closely adapted)

1. **workbuddy2api-panel** (https://github.com/linguo2625469/workbuddy2api-panel)
   MIT License. Original upstream: **Sliverkiss/workbuddy2api**
   (https://github.com/Sliverkiss/workbuddy2api, deleted; attribution preserved).
   Ported/adapted: workbuddy channel error taxonomy and cooldown semantics
   (6004 model-scope / 402 next-4AM / 401 grace / 11101 no-penalty); credit
   cost-tier scheduling and expiring-credit weighting; session stickiness
   semantics; prompt replacement and fingerprint sanitization; credits
   parsing with expiry buckets; growth-task endpoint set and desktop/web
   event-chain shapes (chat / buddy-app / template / playbook / canvas /
   expert summon+use / automation / library); streak redeem & lottery flow;
   buddy adoption/travel flow; request-log metadata discipline.

2. **zcode identity blocks asset**
   `internal/driver/zcode/assets/zcode_system.json` is ported from the same
   MIT project (internal/zcode/gateway/assets/zcode_system.json). The ZCode
   upstream content inspection requires the official client identity blocks.

## Behaviour-level references (no code copied)

3. **AIClient-2-API** (https://github.com/justlovemaki/AIClient-2-API, GPLv3)
   — reverse-engineering knowledge for the Antigravity channel (v1internal
   payload shape, project discovery, quota windows, force-stream handling)
   was used as a behaviour specification only. No GPL code was copied.

4. **sub2api** (https://github.com/Wei-Shaw/sub2api, LGPL-3.0) — session
   fingerprint strategy, three-state admission and 401 grace were adopted as
   patterns (clean-room re-implementation).

5. **CLIProxyAPI** (https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI, MIT) and
   **gemini-openai-proxy** (https://github.com/zhu327/gemini-openai-proxy,
   MIT) — layering and protocol-mapping ideas.

6. **misakano7545/workbuddy2api-panel**
   (https://github.com/misakano7545/workbuddy2api-panel, MIT) — the actively
   maintained line of the same workbuddy2api lineage; later WorkBuddy behaviour
   was checked against it. No code copied beyond what item 1 already covers.

7. **magpie** (https://github.com/yetone/magpie, MIT) — native session-header
   affinity, separating a failure's cause from how long to rest, and repairing
   untyped enums in tool schemas. Re-implemented, no code copied.

8. **magpie-community/plugins** (https://github.com/magpie-community/plugins, MIT),
   packages trae, autoclaw and qoder — the TRAE function ladder
   (chat_v3 / solo_work_lite / solo_agent / solo_agent_lite), the AutoClaw CN
   managed-gateway channel, and the Qoder 10605 queue semantics. Behaviour
   reference only.

9. **qoder2api-hub** (https://github.com/shuishuipingan/qoder2api-hub, MIT) and
   **Trae2api-cn** (https://github.com/autumnsentiment/Trae2api-cn, MIT) —
   Qoder's queued-request protocol, and TRAE model names plus multimodal
   payload shape.

## Behaviour noted, no code taken (upstream has no license)

10. **qoder2api** (https://github.com/Zhengyuuuui/qoder2api) and **autoclaw2api**
